\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 1 \'97 Does this mean we convert semantic meaning into DB filters?\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Yes. That layer is called:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Intent extraction\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Query structuring\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Semantic \uc0\u8594  structured mapping\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The user says:\
\'93Show me non-spicy snacks without peanuts.\'94\
System must extract:\
\
\{\
  heat_level_max: 1,\
  exclude_allergens: ["peanuts"]\
\}\
Then:\
Step 1 \uc0\u8594  SQL metadata filter\u8232 Step 2 \u8594  Vector similarity search inside filtered set\
This is standard RAG architecture in production systems.\
Finding: You are not replacing semantic search. You are 
\f0\b augmenting it with structured constraints
\f1\b0 .\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
