\f0\b \cf0 B) LLM-based query structuring (more powerful)\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 You send the user query to the LLM with a system prompt:\
\'93Extract structured ecommerce filters from this query.\'94\
It returns JSON:\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Goal of Overlap:
\f1\b0  In a real RAG system, you want the overlap to be large enough that any single "fact" (like the $25 fee) is guaranteed to exist 
\f0\b fully
\f1\b0  inside at least one chunk. If your overlap is too small, a fact might get sliced in half, making the vector search "confused" because neither half has the full meaning.\
\
\{\
  "max_heat_level": 1,\
  "exclude_allergens": ["peanuts"],\
  "flavor": null,\
  "max_price": null\
\}\
Then you apply those as SQL filters.\
This is how advanced AI commerce systems operate.\
\

\f0\b C) Hybrid (best practice)\
